{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KaiCHeSz8XJ8HHKuNeDGfm","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t## Task goal\n2\tIndependently verify three small defect fixes on this branch. The pre-build base is commit c4909ee; the fixes are 44ed997 (T-0258), c23fb94 (T-0261), 8ed117d (T-0263). Tickets: .sdlc/0258-fanout-close-ticket-root, .sdlc/0261-split-goal-precheck, .sdlc/0263-stale-lane-route. Each regression test must fail without its fix and pass with it.\n3\t\n4\t## Step 1: Verify the three fixes\n5\tlevel: L3\n6\t\n7\t### Do\n8\t- T-0258: fanout numbered close under `ticket_root: tickets` with `.sdlc/config` untracked (gitignored) failed with `close refused: .sdlc/NNNN-slug/handoff.md: missing or has no front matter`. The fix copies the config into the integration and lane worktrees (plugins/sdlc-lite/scripts/fanout.py). Test: the \"untracked config lane\" case in the fanout selftest.\n9\t- T-0261: `steps.py precheck <task dir>` plus a run.sh refusal (exit 2, before any attempt record) for planner and plan-reviewer when the task handoff has no `## Goal`. Tests: steps.py selftest \"(precheck)\" cases and run-selftest.sh \"goal precheck\".\n10\t- T-0263: `steps.py next` prints `resplit` for a blocked builder whose Notes first line starts `stale lane:`. Also changed: builder.md, chain SKILL, docs/maintenance/sdlc-internals.md, generated Codex builder agents.\n11\tTo show red before, make a throwaway worktree under `$SDLC_TMP_WORKTREES` at HEAD, revert only the non-test hunks of each fix there (the fanout.py config copy block, the run.sh precheck block, the steps.py `stale lane:` branch), and run the matching selftest; say what you did.\n12\t\n13\t### Acceptance criteria\n14\t- `python3 plugins/sdlc-lite/scripts/fanout.py selftest`\n15\t- `python3 plugins/sdlc-lite/scripts/steps.py selftest`\n16\t- `bash plugins/sdlc-lite/scripts/run-selftest.sh`\n17\t- `python3 plugins/sdlc-lite/scripts/check.py`\n18\t- `python3 plugins/sdlc-lite/scripts/codex_roles.py generate --check`\n19\t- `python3 scripts/check-packaging.py`\n20\t- Each of the three regression tests goes red with its fix reverted (observed, not read).\n21\t\n22\t## Builder note\n23\tThe builder (Sonnet) saw red then green for each: fanout selftest printed `merged, close refused: .sdlc/0001-x/handoff.md: missing or has no front matter` before the fix; run-selftest.sh printed `goal precheck: planner on a handoff with no ## Goal exited 0, want 2`; steps selftest failed `next resplit: ...`. Treat these as unverified claims.\n24\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"76368243-d1ff-40cf-98b6-9262e4f17e15","uuid":"b278baf2-ce2e-4b1e-b19a-854560b3847e","timestamp":"2026-10-05T22:33:05.708Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/kimgranlund/Projects/nonoun/sdlc-lite/.claude/worktrees/agent-ae11c915f68bab1f5/.sdlc/verify-defect-fixes-0209/handoff.md","content":"## Task goal\nIndependently verify three small defect fixes on this branch. The pre-build base is commit c4909ee; the fixes are 44ed997 (T-0258), c23fb94 (T-0261), 8ed117d (T-0263). Tickets: .sdlc/0258-fanout-close-ticket-root, .sdlc/0261-split-goal-precheck, .sdlc/0263-stale-lane-route. Each regression test must fail without its fix and pass with it.\n\n## Step 1: Verify the three fixes\nlevel: L3\n\n### Do\n- T-0258: fanout numbered close under `ticket_root: tickets` with `.sdlc/config` untracked (gitignored) failed with `close refused: .sdlc/NNNN-slug/handoff.md: missing or has no front matter`. The fix copies the config into the integration and lane worktrees (plugins/sdlc-lite/scripts/fanout.py). Test: the \"untracked config lane\" case in the fanout selftest.\n- T-0261: `steps.py precheck <task dir>` plus a run.sh refusal (exit 2, before any attempt record) for planner and plan-reviewer when the task handoff has no `## Goal`. Tests: steps.py selftest \"(precheck)\" cases and run-selftest.sh \"goal precheck\".\n- T-0263: `steps.py next` prints `resplit` for a blocked builder whose Notes first line starts `stale lane:`. Also changed: builder.md, chain SKILL, docs/maintenance/sdlc-internals.md, generated Codex builder agents.\nTo show red before, make a throwaway worktree under `$SDLC_TMP_WORKTREES` at HEAD, revert only the non-test hunks of each fix there (the fanout.py config copy block, the run.sh precheck block, the steps.py `stale lane:` branch), and run the matching selftest; say what you did.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- `python3 plugins/sdlc-lite/scripts/fanout.py selftest`\n- `python3 plugins/sdlc-lite/scripts/steps.py selftest`\n- `bash plugins/sdlc-lite/scripts/run-selftest.sh`\n- `python3 plugins/sdlc-lite/scripts/check.py`\n- `python3 plugins/sdlc-lite/scripts/codex_roles.py generate --check`\n- `python3 scripts/check-packaging.py`\n- Each of the three regression tests goes red with its fix reverted (observed, not read).\n\n## Builder note\nThe builder (Sonnet) saw red then green for each: fanout selftest printed `merged, close refused: .sdlc/0001-x/handoff.md: missing or has no front matter` before the fix; run-selftest.sh printed `goal precheck: planner on a handoff with no ## Goal exited 0, want 2`; steps selftest failed `next resplit: ...`. Treat these as unverified claims.\n","numLines":24,"startLine":1,"totalLines":24}}}
