{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Do5T7o9jeuKEBhzjYkqyQX","type":"tool_result","content":"commit 8ed117dd69dc3d91a009f038df16ca1785bbe28f\nAuthor: Kim Granlund <kim.granlund@gmail.com>\nDate:   Mon Oct 5 15:31:40 2026 -0700\n\n    T-0263: steps.py next routes a stale-lane block to resplit, not replan\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\ndiff --git a/plugins/sdlc-lite/scripts/steps.py b/plugins/sdlc-lite/scripts/steps.py\nindex ed1d65a..8e62b18 100755\n--- a/plugins/sdlc-lite/scripts/steps.py\n+++ b/plugins/sdlc-lite/scripts/steps.py\n@@ -205,7 +205,9 @@ Usage: steps.py {split <planner.md | task dir> [--only N ...] [--guard-timeout S\n               newest builder Status inherited red: <tests> -> inherited (a gate already red at\n                 the pre-build HEAD; ask the conductor). Never counted as a fail, a bump, a\n                 rebuild, or a replan; a bare \"inherited red\" with no colon is statusless.\n-              newest builder Status blocked              -> replan (whatever its Notes say)\n+              newest builder Status blocked              -> replan (whatever its Notes say), except Notes whose\n+                first line starts \"stale lane:\" (missing merged prerequisites, not a plan defect) -> resplit:\n+                rebase the lane, move the step dir to step-<n>.superseded-<k>, steps.py split --only <n>\n               no verifier result counts after the build  -> verify L<verifier level>,\n                 but done when batch_verified(step dir) names a task-dir verifier result: the\n                 newest task-dir verifier-*.md (order.py) whose ## Verified section lists\n@@ -1267,6 +1269,14 @@ def next_action(step_dir):\n                 'ask the conductor, not a fail, rebuild, bump, or replan', read)\n     builders = [x for x in builders if build_status_or_none(x) in ('done', 'blocked')]\n     if build_status(b) == 'blocked':\n+        notes = section(b, 'Notes') or []\n+        first = next((line.strip() for line in notes if line.strip()), '')\n+        if first.startswith('stale lane:'):\n+            n = re.sub(r'^step-(\\d+)$', r'\\1', d.name)\n+            return ('resplit', None,\n+                    f'newest builder {os.path.basename(b)} is blocked by a stale lane, not a plan defect ({first}); '\n+                    f'rebase the lane onto the merged prerequisites, move {d.name} to {d.name}.superseded-<k> '\n+                    f'(next free k), then steps.py split --only {n} <task dir>; never a replan', read)\n         return 'replan', None, f'newest builder {os.path.basename(b)} is blocked (a blocked build replans)', read\n     v = order.newest(d, 'verifier')\n     if v is None or not order.counts_after(v, b):\n@@ -2780,6 +2790,11 @@ def selftest():\n               nxt(step(3, [('builder-L3.md', DONE)]), 'verify L2'))\n         check('next replan: a blocked builder replans, whatever its Notes say',\n               nxt(step(2, [('builder-L2.md', BLOCKED)]), 'replan'))\n+        STALE = '## Status\\nblocked\\n\\n## Notes\\nstale lane: T-0042 is not merged into this lane\\n'\n+        rc, out, err = run_main(['next', str(step(2, [('builder-L2.md', STALE)]))])\n+        check('next resplit: a blocked builder whose Notes start \"stale lane:\" routes to resplit, not replan, '\n+              'naming .superseded and split --only',\n+              rc == 0 and out.splitlines()[:1] == ['resplit'] and '.superseded-' in out and 'split --only' in out)\n         check('next replan: a fail whose next-attempt note starts \"plan defect:\" replans',\n               nxt(step(2, [('builder-L2.md', DONE), ('verifier-L1.md', DEFECT)]), 'replan'))\n         check('next done: the newest verifier passed',\n=== builder.md\n--- a/plugins/sdlc-lite/agents/builder.md\n+++ b/plugins/sdlc-lite/agents/builder.md\n-3. If the step cannot be done as specified, stop and say why. Do not improvise a different step. When the step cannot pass because a criterion is defective (it does not parse, contradicts another criterion, or is wrong on its face), Status is blocked and the first line of Notes is `plan defect: <criterion> <why>`. Leave the work done so far in the tree and say so in Notes. Never report done with a defective criterion left for the verifier.\n+3. If the step cannot be done as specified, stop and say why. Do not improvise a different step. When the step cannot pass because a criterion is defective (it does not parse, contradicts another criterion, or is wrong on its face), Status is blocked and the first line of Notes is `plan defect: <criterion> <why>`. Leave the work done so far in the tree and say so in Notes. Never report done with a defective criterion left for the verifier. When the step is blocked only because prerequisites it builds on are not in this tree (an earlier ticket or step not yet merged), Status is blocked and the\n=== chain SKILL\n--- a/plugins/sdlc-lite/skills/chain/SKILL.md\n+++ b/plugins/sdlc-lite/skills/chain/SKILL.md\n-After each builder run and each verifier run, run `python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/steps.py next .sdlc/<task>/step-<n>` and follow the action on its first line: `build`, `rebuild`, or `bump` → builder at that level; `verify` or `reverify` → verifier at that level; `replan` → the 4.2 path; `swap` → run `python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/steps.py swap .sdlc/<task>/step-<n>`: exit 0 → append one line `swap applied: step <n>: <its stdout line>` to the task handoff's `## Plan review` (create it if missing, keep earlier entries) and run the builder at the level `next` printed (a rebuild: no `## Previous attempt`, never a bump, never counted toward \"a second fail\"); exit 1 → append its stderr to `## Plan review` and take the 4.2 replan path; `done` → next step; `stop` → ask the user; `inherited` → the gate was already red at the pre-build HEAD (builder Status `inherited red: <tests>`\n+After each builder run and each verifier run, run `python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/steps.py next .sdlc/<task>/step-<n>` and follow the action on its first line: `build`, `rebuild`, or `bump` → builder at that level; `verify` or `reverify` → verifier at that level; `replan` → the 4.2 path; `resplit` (a builder blocked with Notes starting `stale lane:`, meaning merged prerequisites are missing from the lane and the plan is sound) → rebase the lane onto them, rename the step dir to `step-<n>.superseded-<k>` (next free k), run `steps.py split --only <n> .sdlc/<task>`, and rerun the builder; it is never a replan and costs no planner run; `swap` → run `python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/steps.py swap .sdlc/<task>/step-<n>`: exit 0 → append one line `swap applied: step <n>: <its stdout line>` to the task handoff's `## Plan review` (create it if missing, keep earlier entries) and run t\n=== internals\nstale lane:` (merged prerequisites missing from the lane, not a plan defect, T-0263) maps to `resplit`, never `replan`: rebase the lane onto the prerequisites, move the step dir to `step-<n>.\n=== toml l1\nstale lane: <what is missing>`.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"76368243-d1ff-40cf-98b6-9262e4f17e15","uuid":"a97353b9-afb3-4e51-9c7f-a197d7a09e02","timestamp":"2026-10-05T22:33:32.412Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"commit 8ed117dd69dc3d91a009f038df16ca1785bbe28f\nAuthor: Kim Granlund <kim.granlund@gmail.com>\nDate:   Mon Oct 5 15:31:40 2026 -0700\n\n    T-0263: steps.py next routes a stale-lane block to resplit, not replan\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\ndiff --git a/plugins/sdlc-lite/scripts/steps.py b/plugins/sdlc-lite/scripts/steps.py\nindex ed1d65a..8e62b18 100755\n--- a/plugins/sdlc-lite/scripts/steps.py\n+++ b/plugins/sdlc-lite/scripts/steps.py\n@@ -205,7 +205,9 @@ Usage: steps.py {split <planner.md | task dir> [--only N ...] [--guard-timeout S\n               newest builder Status inherited red: <tests> -> inherited (a gate already red at\n                