steps.py split` fails fast, before any planner or reviewer runs, when the task handoff lacks `## Goal`.\n\n## Context\n`steps.py split` requires `## Goal` in the task handoff (`read_goal`). Four planner runs and four plan reviews were spent (about 2 hours, maison T-0105) before a handoff using `## Task goal` was caught at split.\nFix: a precheck with a clear message that names the missing heading, run where a planner would be launched (steps.py lint/plan entry), and a regression test showing it fails before and passes after.\n\n## Constraints\nNo push, tag, version bump, or publish. No em dashes.\n=== T-0263\n---\nid: T-0263\ntitle: \"A builder blocked by a stale lane routes to replan, not rebase-and-resplit\"\ntype: bug             # feature | bug | chore | spike | idea\nstatus: proposed     # proposed | ready | blocked | done | dropped (build progress lives in /board)\nsize: S              # S | M | L | XL\npriority: P2         # P1 | P2 | P3\ndepends: []          # T-NNNN, file:<path>, cap:<name>; e.g. [T-0002]\ncreated: 2026-10-05\nrouter: .sdlc/AGENTS.md  # how to claim and close this ticket\n---\n\n## Goal\nA blocked builder whose cause is a stale lane (missing merged prerequisites, not a plan defect) has a named route: rebase and resplit the step.\n\n## Context\n`steps.py next` prints `replan` for a block whose cause is a stale lane. The right route is rebase the lane onto its merged prerequisites, move the step dir to `.superseded-N`, then `steps.py split --only N`.\nFix: route or message in steps.py naming that, documented in `docs/maintenance/sdlc-internals.md`, with a regression test.\n\n## Constraints\nNo push, tag, version bump, or publish. No em dashes.\n=== builder.md full changed line\nugrep: error: error at position 5\n(?m)^+++\n     \\___invalid syntax","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"76368243-d1ff-40cf-98b6-9262e4f17e15","uuid":"534b7abb-ba27-45b2-ae87-498eeebebfc1","timestamp":"2026-10-05T22:33:41.533Z","tool_use_resul